IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-amount`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), sections 37 to 40 and 42 -- DEBTS AND
-- OVERPAYMENTS, AND THE DAY THE REGULATIONS CAME INTO FORCE.
--
-- The Regulations name no rate of interest, so "interest is payable" is a yes or no, never a
-- sum. Section 41 amends the Social Security Tribunal Regulations, 2022 and its text is
-- shown here only as "[Amendments]": it is blank in this text.

§ `Regulations s 37 -- Return of benefit`

-- 37(1): a person or agency that received a benefit payment it was not entitled to, or more
-- than it was entitled to, must return the amount of the erroneous payment or the overpayment
-- as soon as feasible. The amount is what was paid less what was due, and nothing if that is
-- not positive.
-- src:326 | 37 (1) A person or agency that has received a benefit payment to which the person or agency is not entitled, or that has received a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit to which the person or agency is entitled, must return the amount of the erroneous payment or the overpayment, as the case may be, as soon as feasible.
@ref Regulations s 37(1) (src:326)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit payments received` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit the person or agency was entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount that must be returned` `the amount of the benefit payments received` `the amount of the benefit the person or agency was entitled to` MEANS
    `the larger number of` 0 (`the amount of the benefit payments received` MINUS `the amount of the benefit the person or agency was entitled to`)

-- 37(2): the amount is a debt due to His Majesty in right of Canada as of the day it was
-- paid, which the Minister may recover. NOTHING when there is no erroneous payment or
-- overpayment.
-- src:328 | (2) The amount of the erroneous payment or overpayment constitutes a debt due to His Majesty in right of Canada, as of the day on which it was paid, that may be recovered by the Minister.
@ref Regulations s 37(2) (src:328)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit payments received` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit the person or agency was entitled to` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the payment was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day from which the erroneous payment or overpayment is a debt due to His Majesty` `the amount of the benefit payments received` `the amount of the benefit the person or agency was entitled to` `the day the payment was made` MEANS
    IF `the amount that must be returned` `the amount of the benefit payments received` `the amount of the benefit the person or agency was entitled to` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST `the day the payment was made`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 37(3): the debt may be paid in one payment or, if the Minister agrees, in instalments of any
-- amount that does not cause undue hardship.
-- src:330 | (3) A debt recoverable from a person under this section may be paid as a single payment or, if the Minister agrees, in instalments in any amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person.
@ref Regulations s 37(3) (src:330)
GIVEN `the Minister agrees to instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each instalment is an amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the debt may be paid in instalments` `the Minister agrees to instalments` `each instalment is an amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person` MEANS
        `the Minister agrees to instalments`
    AND `each instalment is an amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person`

-- 37(4) and 37(5): no interest on an amount owing from an erroneous payment or overpayment,
-- except that where the payment was made as a result of a violation for which a penalty was
-- imposed under s 35, or an offence for which a fine or imprisonment was imposed, the no-interest
-- rule applies only while a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or
-- appeal can be made, or is pending. Outside that period interest is payable on such an amount.
-- src:332 | (4) No interest is payable on any amount owing to His Majesty in right of Canada under the Act or these Regulations that results from an erroneous payment or overpayment.
-- src:333 | Exception
-- src:334 | (5) In the case of an amount owing to His Majesty in right of Canada that results from a payment that was made as a result of a violation for which a penalty was imposed under section 35 or as a result of an offence under subsection 36(1) for which a fine or a term of imprisonment was imposed under the Criminal Code, subsection (4) applies only during any period in which
-- src:335 | (a) a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made with respect to the violation or offence; or
-- src:336 | (b) the reconsideration, judicial review or appeal is pending.
@ref Regulations s 37(4) and (5) (src:332-336)
GIVEN `the payment was made as a result of a violation for which a penalty was imposed under section 35 or an offence for which a fine or a term of imprisonment was imposed under the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made, or is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`interest is payable on the amount owing` `the payment was made as a result of a violation for which a penalty was imposed under section 35 or an offence for which a fine or a term of imprisonment was imposed under the Criminal Code` `a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made, or is pending` MEANS
        `the payment was made as a result of a violation for which a penalty was imposed under section 35 or an offence for which a fine or a term of imprisonment was imposed under the Criminal Code`
    AND NOT `a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made, or is pending`

§ `Regulations s 38 -- Recovery of penalties`

-- 38(1): a penalty is a debt due to His Majesty as of the day it was imposed.
-- src:338 | 38 (1) A penalty imposed under section 35 constitutes a debt due to His Majesty in right of Canada, as of the day on which it was imposed, that may be recovered by the Minister.
@ref Regulations s 38(1) (src:338)
GIVEN `the day the penalty was imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day from which a penalty is a debt due to His Majesty` `the day the penalty was imposed` MEANS
    `the day the penalty was imposed`

-- 38(2): interest on the debt does not accrue while a request for reconsideration, application
-- for judicial review or appeal can be made about the decision to impose the penalty or its
-- amount, or is pending.
-- src:340 | (2) Interest on the debt does not accrue during any period in which
-- src:341 | (a) a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made with respect to the decision to impose a penalty or the decision as to the amount of the penalty; or
-- src:342 | (b) the reconsideration, judicial review or appeal is pending.
@ref Regulations s 38(2) (src:340-342)
GIVEN `a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made, or is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`interest accrues on the penalty debt` `a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made, or is pending` MEANS
    NOT `a request for reconsideration, application for judicial review or appeal can be made, or is pending`

§ `Regulations s 39 -- Limitation period or prescription`

-- 39(1) and 39(2): no action to recover money after the end of the six-year period that
-- begins on the day the money becomes due and payable, which stops running while an action is
-- prohibited or a review of the decision establishing liability is pending. A period that begins
-- on a day ends on the day before the sixth anniversary of it, and each suspended day moves the
-- end back by one day (fork F16). The last day is returned.
-- src:344 | 39 (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), no action or proceedings may be taken to recover money owing under the Act or these Regulations after the end of the six-year limitation period or prescription that begins on the day on which the money becomes due and payable.
-- src:345 | Limitation period or prescription suspended
-- src:346 | (2) The running of a limitation period or prescription is suspended during any period in which
-- src:347 | (a) it is prohibited to commence or continue an action or other proceedings against the debtor to recover money owing under the Act or these Regulations; or
-- src:348 | (b) a review of a decision establishing liability in respect of money owing under the Act or these Regulations is pending.
@ref Regulations s 39(1) and (2) (src:344-348)
GIVEN `the day the money becomes due and payable` IS A DATE
      `the number of days during which the running of the period was suspended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day on which an action to recover money may be taken` `the day the money becomes due and payable` `the number of days during which the running of the period was suspended` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the day the money becomes due and payable`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the money becomes due and payable`) (DATE_YEAR `the day the money becomes due and payable` PLUS 6) MINUS 1 PLUS `the number of days during which the running of the period was suspended`

-- 39(3): the limitation period does not apply to execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment.
-- src:350 | (3) This section does not apply in respect of an action or proceedings relating to the execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment.
@ref Regulations s 39(3) (src:350)
GIVEN `the proceedings relate to the execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the six-year limitation period applies` `the proceedings relate to the execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment` MEANS
    NOT `the proceedings relate to the execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment`

§ `Regulations s 40 -- Certificates`

-- 40(1): an unrecovered debt may be certified without delay if the Minister is of the opinion
-- that the debtor is attempting to avoid payment, and otherwise 30 days after the day the
-- default occurred. The earliest day of certification is returned.
-- src:352 | 40 (1) All or part of the debt that has not been recovered may be certified by the Minister
-- src:353 | (a) without delay, if, in the Minister’s opinion, the debtor is attempting to avoid payment; and
-- src:354 | (b) 30 days after the day on which the default occurred, in any other case.
@ref Regulations s 40(1) (src:352-354)
GIVEN `the day the default occurred` IS A DATE
      `in the Minister's opinion the debtor is attempting to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day on which the unrecovered debt may be certified` `the day the default occurred` `in the Minister's opinion the debtor is attempting to avoid payment` MEANS
    IF `in the Minister's opinion the debtor is attempting to avoid payment`
    THEN `the day the default occurred`
    ELSE `the day the default occurred` PLUS 30

-- 40(6): garnishment. If the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to
-- become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person who owes money to His Majesty under
-- the Act or the Regulations, the Minister may, by a notice served personally or by confirmed
-- delivery service, require the first person to pay the money to the Receiver General.
-- src:364 | (6) If the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to His Majesty in right of Canada under the Act or these Regulations, the Minister may, by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person in whole or in part to the Receiver General on account of the second person’s liability.
@ref Regulations s 40(6) (src:364)
GIVEN `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to His Majesty under the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may require the money to be paid to the Receiver General` `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to His Majesty under the Act or these Regulations` `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` MEANS
        `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to His Majesty under the Act or these Regulations`
    AND `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service`

-- 40(7): an amount not paid as required by such a notice is a debt due to His Majesty.
-- src:366 | (7) An amount not paid as required by a notice under subsection (6) is a debt due to His Majesty in right of Canada.
@ref Regulations s 40(7) (src:366)
GIVEN `the amount was required to be paid by a notice under subsection 40(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was not paid as the notice required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the unpaid amount is a debt due to His Majesty` `the amount was required to be paid by a notice under subsection 40(6)` `the amount was not paid as the notice required` MEANS
        `the amount was required to be paid by a notice under subsection 40(6)`
    AND `the amount was not paid as the notice required`

§ `Regulations s 42 -- Coming into Force`

-- 42: the Regulations came into force on May 15, 2025. A date, carried as a value.
-- src:373 | 42 These Regulations come into force on May 15, 2025.
@ref Regulations s 42 (src:373)
`the day the Regulations come into force` MEANS YMD 2025 5 15
